  "_comment": "Ticket 26/09/02/SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION: split out of the former `✳️any` catch-all. The GIF89a Specification (CompuServe, 1990) §26 defines the Application Extension as a self-contained, optional block (block label 0x21 0xFF) identifying an 11-byte application identifier/auth-code plus opaque application sub-blocks -- the mechanism `add-app-extension`/`remove-app-extension` expose directly, and that the de-facto NETSCAPE2.0 looping sub-block (`set-loop-count`) is layered on top of. All three are owned here rather than by `✳️base`, for the same family-module reuse rationale as `../../✳️graphic-control/🧪️oracle/🔣️.json`.",
